WEBVTT

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.730 --> 00:02:02.150
The Duelist
Chapter III

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.000
In January of Imperial Year 483...

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.160
...the duel between the
Helksheimers and the Schafhausens...

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:19.070
...was about to begin in an arena made available for the contest by the Marquis of Littenheim.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.800
Thank you for letting us use such a nice arena for this odd little event.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.170
Don't mention it.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.170
I'm happy to do this anytime.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.980
By the way, where is
the little lady today ?

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:41.990
I can't allow her to view this vulgar
bloodshed by these low-born people.

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:45.330
The future Kaiserin{Empress}, correct ?

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:46.250
Huh ?

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:00.900
What's the meaning of this ?

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.900
Why are they in a luxury sky box...

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:05.720
...while we're down here in
General Admission seating ?

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.650
An honorable duel is supposed to be carried out on equal terms, is it not ?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.200
I'm betting 10,000 on the Helksheimers !

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.720
Will no one bet on
the Schafhausens ?

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.470
Are there no real
gamblers among you ?

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.780
So that's the brat we've
been hearing about.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.980
Like his sister, his face
alone is quite handsome.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.450
Your duelist has changed
from the one I saw before ?

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.540
There was a minuscule inconvenience...

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:50.450
...but he is even more
skilled than my usual agent.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.950
Please be assured.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.660
But he seems to lack flamboyance.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:01.500
Doesn't he have enough charm
to at least wave to the spectators ?

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.620
See, the spectators are
already rather unimpressed.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.530
I'll tell him that later.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:22.960
Do your best !

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:34.910
That Baroness, she's too
much for us, isn't she ?

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.550
You were quite thorough.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:17.400
I've heard Count Helksheimer is a sly individual.

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.800
I had to make sure that
the pistols weren't fixed.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:23.090
Kircheis, you're so cautious.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:24.900
I trust in you.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:31.950
Lord Reinhard.

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:37.220
I have a suggestion,
so will you listen to me ?

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:37.900
What is it ?

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.850
Duelists assume that, after facing in
opposite directions and walking away...

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:46.280
...they're supposed to fire from that exact spot when they turn back to face their opponent.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:50.720
But according to the rules,
there is no such restriction.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:51.540
So ?

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.750
So at the time of the shot...

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:58.400
...you should jump to either your right or left, and evade your opponent's aim.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.800
Isn't that unfair ?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.150
Your opponent is
a professional duelist.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.190
I would think a simple tactic
like this would be permissible.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:11.900
But from that posture, it'll be
difficult for me to take aim as well.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:16.970
So you'll be prepared to determine the fight with the second shot.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.760
Your first shot, while jumping away,
only serves to keep your opponent at bay.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.900
Your opponent would be perplexed
by your unexpected movement...

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.250
...and if he were to be shot from that position he would be even more perturbed.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.940
Then it would be highly likely that he would miss with his shot.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.150
Because your opponent is an expert...

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:36.640
...he must be planning to decide
the fight with his first shot.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.600
But if he misses, that would unsettle him further, and carry over to his next shot.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:47.700
On the other hand, if you're prepared to
make the second shot the decisive one...

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.860
I have the psychological advantage, it seems.

00:06:57.130 --> 00:06:58.050
No, I can't.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:03.650
If I fight in a manner that might
in any way be held in contempt...

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.410
...I could tarnish the name
of the Schafhausens.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.190
That would defeat the purpose{of fighting the duel}.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:13.600
But, Lord Reinhard, I must repeat that your opponent is an expert.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.260
If you're going to just fire at each other, you are at a disadvantage.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:17.670
In this instance, please...

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:18.740
Both sides, come forward !

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:45.170
What is this unsettling feeling ?

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:49.400
If there is such a thing as a God of Death, it might look like this man.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:54.950
Would a duelist reek
so much of death ?

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:02.150
Based on the prior arrangements,
the duel will be carried out with pistols.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:04.500
No objections from 
either side, I presume ?

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:10.300
You will each be armed with two single shot pistols, and after standing back to back...

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.280
...you will take ten steps, and then you will turn around and fire at each other.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:17.510
The one who robs the other of his ability or will to fight will be proclaimed the winner.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:22.830
If the duel cannot be resolved with pistols,
the winner will be determined with swords.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:23.650
Understood ?

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.150
I accept.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:27.950
No objections.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:44.320
Now the duel between the Helksheimers
and the Schafhausens will be carried out...

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.970
...by the hands of agents
from the respective sides.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.170
The outcome of this duel will resolve
the dispute between the two families...

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:54.190
...and no grudge may be held in regard to the outcome.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:56.340
Now, both of you
take your positions !

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:34.190
Because my opponent is an expert...

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.450
One !

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.500
Two !

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.340
Three !

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.240
Four !

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:56.360
Five !

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:00.510
Six !

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.000
Seven !

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:09.410
Eight !

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:13.780
Nine !

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.480
Your opponent is an expert !

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.140
I must do what's necessary.

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:23.370
Ten !

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:42.860
Lord Reinhard !

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.730
What the heck is this ?

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:15.850
This is spoiling the fun.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:17.710
You did it !

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:18.680
We won !

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:27.090
Lord Reinhard, may I see your wound ?

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:28.230
It's not serious.

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:36.190
I'm glad the injury poses
 no risk to your life.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:38.730
But I feared my life
would be shortened.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:45.000
Thanks to your advice.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.250
And Lt Commander Lutz, wasn't it ?

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:51.930
I was saved because he advised me
to put my left arm in front of my body.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:55.020
Otherwise, I would have been
shot in the left side of my chest.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.040
Damn.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:20.410
The agent of the Helksheimers 
was wounded in the right shoulder...

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:24.410
...the agent of the
Schafhausens, left arm.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.070
Therefore, the Schafhausens will be...

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:28.080
Hold it !

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:32.380
I wish to continue with swords.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.430
Good !

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:37.500
That's the way !

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:01.730
Let him do it !

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:04.580
No one's satisfied with
this outcome anyway !

00:13:05.710 --> 00:13:07.460
What's going to happen ?

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:10.300
As long as his opponent is
willing to fight, he can't refuse.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.800
Agent of the Schafhausens,
what will you do ?

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:16.090
I willingly accept the challenge !

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:17.260
Wait.

00:13:17.260 --> 00:13:19.260
Before that, I must make
a demand as his second.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.000
I'd like to treat his wound.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.620
Lord Reinhard, please be careful.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.110
What is it ?

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.590
Normally, the duel would be over as it is.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.740
His persistence is unusual.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.260
All right.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:46.200
I grant permission for both
sides to treat their wounds.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:47.830
What am I going to do ?

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:49.650
I let him get injured...

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:51.430
Annerose might be upset with me.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.030
It must be around here !

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:55.110
Look more closely !

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:58.790
Hey, what are you doing ?

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:01.800
Well, the betting slips we just threw away are somewhere around here.

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:05.060
You're like pigs after slop.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.670
Fortunately, the bullet
didn't reach the bone.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:11.410
It stopped in the muscle.

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:22.000
I'm grateful it was an old-fashioned pistol with little penetrative force.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:26.750
But if you had been shot in the chest, it would have reached your heart.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:29.240
In that case, it would've
been a fatal injury.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.360
I know.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:36.570
Did his shot get away by accident,
or did he intentionally aim at your chest ?

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:41.180
That's what you meant by "be careful."

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:45.400
It would be prudent to assume the "safety" no longer exists.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.660
This has become a
life-and-death battle.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.940
Kircheis.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.970
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:04.770
There was something we
made a pledge about before.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:08.950
We will never lose,
at any time, to any enemy.

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.330
Lord Reinhard...

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.100
All right.

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:21.050
Are you going to be okay ?

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:22.270
Don't worry.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.150
Besides, I'll be using the
sword with my right hand.

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:26.560
That guy{the opponent} has hurt his right arm.

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.650
I definitely won't be defeated.

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.190
Kircheis, give me the sword.

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:38.210
Both sides, come forward !

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.250
I'm glad.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.450
He looks okay.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:10.990
Lord Reinhard !

00:16:10.990 --> 00:16:12.090
I'm okay.

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:13.580
I'd forgotten that I was injured.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:22.980
I would suspect his injury is worse than mine, but I don't want to prolong the fight.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:28.210
Moreover, if he intends to kill me,
I have to be prepared to do the same.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.430
Cross your swords !

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:41.650
Commence !

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.900
What is he ?

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:15.090
He fired the gun with his right hand,
so I thought he was right-handed...

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:17.720
...but he's really skilled
with his left hand, too.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.750
Lord Reinhard is being
pushed to the limit.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.260
That man - sword fighting
seems to be his real forte.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:32.250
Moreover, he's not aiming for
the hand - he's going for the kill.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:38.270
Good !

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:38.720
There !

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:39.660
Go for it !

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:40.590
Go ahead !

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:42.270
Slice up his face with a scar or two !

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:51.600
Lord Reinhard...

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:06.190
Hold !  Hold !

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:10.140
Stop the duel !

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:12.400
What's happening ?

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:13.700
Who dares to enter my
manor without permission ?

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.070
They're Imperial Guards.

00:18:18.380 --> 00:18:19.960
Both sides, lower your swords !

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:21.900
This is a special order.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:26.310
By order of the Kaiser,
this duel must be suspended.

00:18:28.180 --> 00:18:29.100
Suspended ?

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:34.030
Annerose must have
gotten to the Kaiser.

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:36.900
Lord Reinhard.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.830
Kircheis !

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.160
Lord Reinhard, I understand.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:46.170
I understand, so please
bear with it for now...

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:50.380
What do you mean "suspended" ?

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:51.950
What's going to happen
to the mining rights ?

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:56.840
It's the decision
of the Kaiser himself.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:58.300
The duel must be suspended...

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:01.860
...and the mining rights must be split in half between the two parties.

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:03.480
Split ?

00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:04.690
Ridiculous !

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:07.200
If the duel had continued,
we would have won !

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:10.020
How am I supposed to
be satisfied with a split ?

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.450
It's the decision of the Kaiser !

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:16.810
In the Empire, the Kaiser's decisions
take precedence over any law !

00:19:16.810 --> 00:19:19.500
If you do not intend to obey,
it will be considered treason !

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.300
Understood ?

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:22.900
T...treason ?

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.310
I have no choice...

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.700
How about the Schafhausens ?

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:39.640
Of course, we thank
His Majesty for his decision.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:43.560
Then we acknowledge there
is no objection from either side.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:45.910
As it stands now, this
dispute has been resolved.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:48.520
We expect no further argument in regards to this matter.

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.680
Lieutenant Musel, are you all right ?

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:58.930
Yes, it's nothing serious.

00:19:58.930 --> 00:20:01.060
I'm sorry that I couldn't
be of much use.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:02.860
Not at all.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:06.210
As things stood, we would
have lost all of our mining rights.

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:10.190
We now have half, and it's all because
of the Lieutenant's accomplishment.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:15.140
And Annerose must have
reached the Kaiser.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:17.000
We thank you both.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:28.500
Well, Lord Reinhard, let's go to the
hospital to get you properly treated.

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:30.770
A...all right.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:33.110
I have a limousine ready.

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:34.110
Why don't you use it ?

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.480
Thank you.

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:38.130
We gladly accept your offer.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.600
I'm sorry.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:46.240
I didn't think it would be
this dangerous for you.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:51.490
But that duelist, it's strange that
he fought with such a vengeance.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.700
Yeah, that man !

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:02.340
I hired him because he said he
was good, but how disgraceful !

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:06.470
He couldn't even beat an amateur
brat, and he's embarrassed me !

00:21:06.470 --> 00:21:08.160
Get him over here !

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.410
I'll give him a proper punishment !

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:14.470
But...he can't be found anywhere.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:16.220
What ?

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:18.650
It seems he's vanished.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:35.650
Lord Reinhard, your opponent
seems to have disappeared.

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:39.240
I would hope such a dangerous
man would vanish forever.

00:21:39.810 --> 00:21:42.390
Oh, you sound unusually weak-spirited.

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:44.740
It's not that.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:47.270
It's not that, but...

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:48.300
...I'm exhausted.

00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:52.960
We're ready.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:59.830
Kircheis, let me lean on your shoulder.

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.780
Wake me up when we get there.

00:22:08.730 --> 00:22:11.600
My goodness.
He really is exhausted.

00:22:14.450 --> 00:22:17.110
In this manner, the affair
came to its conclusion.

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:20.590
That is what Reinhard and Kircheis believed.

00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:21.260
But...

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:32.800
Tell the Marchioness I will complete the task she requested, at any cost.

00:22:35.550 --> 00:22:39.240
And this time around, I'll do it my way.

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:41.960
So don't interfere with me.

00:22:42.960 --> 00:22:44.170
Understood ?

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:02.620
The danger has not yet passed.

00:23:00.500 --> 00:23:04.250
To be continued

00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:14.520
[ The Promised Future ]

00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:14.520
End Theme

00:23:09.520 --> 00:23:14.520
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:19.660
Reinhard:

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:19.660
Horikawa Ryu

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:24.160
Magdalena:

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:24.160
Yooko Mari

00:23:20.060 --> 00:23:23.830
Somewhere, the stars...

00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:28.870
...must be looking to...

00:23:24.430 --> 00:23:28.670
Littenheim:

00:23:24.430 --> 00:23:28.670
Terashima Mikio

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:33.370
...the promised future

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:37.710
Narrator:

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:37.710
Yara Yuusaku

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:38.080
I don't count on...

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:43.320
...luck

00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:47.990
Inside this heart of mine...

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:52.130
...I have the determination...

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:53.280
Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:55.600
...to carry the weight of glory

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:59.280
Timing:
Todd Perkins

